The Docker Hub images of the Docker labs, saved by `make -C images docker-hub-images` (one
`docker save` tarball per image, named after its tag: nginx_1.29-alpine.tar...) and copied into
the devops13 image (/usr/local/share/sre-docker-images/): the lab containers have no Internet access, their
inner Docker daemon loads these files.  The target pulls through the Docker daemon of the build
host, so its registry mirror and proxy apply; a file already here is kept (remove it to fetch the
image again).

Optionally, the Debian packages of Docker's repository, for a build host that cannot reach
download.docker.com (the room workstations when their Internet access is off):

  docker-ce_<version>_amd64.deb  docker-ce-cli_<version>_amd64.deb  containerd.io_<version>_amd64.deb
  docker-buildx-plugin_<version>_amd64.deb  docker-compose-plugin_<version>_amd64.deb
                                        https://download.docker.com/linux/debian/dists/trixie/pool/stable/amd64/

The directory is otherwise empty; the files are not committed (.gitignore).

The images of the Kubernetes lab that the Docker labs do not use (KUBE_HUB_IMAGES of
images/Makefile: traefik/whoami) are saved by the same target into kube/.

Optionally, for a build host that cannot reach GitHub, the k3s release files in k3s/ (named as in
the release, checked against the sha256 of the Dockerfile; K3S_VERSION there):

  k3s  k3s-airgap-images-amd64.tar.zst            (arm64: k3s-arm64  k3s-airgap-images-arm64.tar.zst)
                                        https://github.com/k3s-io/k3s/releases/tag/<K3S_VERSION>
